course: dictionary
lesson: 2935
title: Dreadful: bad, scary or very
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence shows you which one to use. «Dreadful» can mean very bad, as in «dreadful weather», or it can mean something that makes you afraid.
explain: Look at the words near it. In «a dreadful mistake», the mistake is bad and has serious results, so dreadful means very bad. The old rhyme warns that people who take cakes «makes dreadful mistakes», so the bad result is the point.
explain: Sometimes «dreadful» is just a booster, as in «a dreadful mess». It means very, not scary. Try swapping in very or terrible. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Dreadful means very bad or unpleasant.
fact: Dreadful can also mean causing fear or great shock, like terrible.
fact: In everyday talk, dreadful can make something stronger: «a dreadful mess» means a very big mess.
fact: French has a funny weather phrase: a dreadful stormy day is «un temps de chien», which means "a dog's weather".
fact: The phrase «dreadful mistakes» in the old rhyme is a warning that bad choices can lead to serious trouble.
exercise: «The weather was dreadful all week, with rain every day.» What does dreadful mean here? | *Very bad | Very far away | Very tasty | Very quiet
exercise: «The dreadful news made the whole village go silent.» What does dreadful suggest? | Something that smells nice | Something very funny | Something that is very small | *Something that causes fear or great shock
exercise: In «There was a dreadful mess in the kitchen», dreadful is a booster. What does it make the mess? | Frightening, like a ghost | Wet and cold | *Very big, a really bad mess | Asleep under the table
test: «I feel dreadful, so I am staying in bed.» What does dreadful mean here? | *Ill or very unwell | Hungry for dinner | Excited about a trip | Very tall
test: Which sentence uses dreadful to mean causing fear? | We ate a dreadful cake for lunch | I felt dreadful after the long bus ride | *A dreadful howl echoed through the dark forest | Our dreadful dog likes to swim
exam: What does «a dreadful mistake» tell us about the mistake? | *It was very bad, with serious results | Funny and small | Hidden in a box | Happy and fun
